  "history": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "Fang Yuan receives this grass Gu among the family assets the internal affairs hall returns after his asset mission on Qing Mao Mountain.",
        "chapters": [
          102
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "intro",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_fang_yuan",
          "loc_qing_mao_mountain"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Before Fang Yuan, his uncle Gu Yue Dong Tu held this grass Gu and sold vitality leaves, which is why Dong Tu kept outside influence as a retired “hidden elder.”",
        "chapters": [
          102
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "ownership-on-qing-mao-mountain",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_gu_yue_dong_tu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Fang Yuan keeps it as the most valuable part of the inheritance for healing and stone income, and that income helps feed the other Gu he raises.",
        "chapters": [
          106
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "ownership-on-qing-mao-mountain",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "The Gu Yue clan also holds five Nine Leaf Vitality Grass Gu as collective property, with specialized Gu Masters tasked to produce vitality leaves every day. Other villagers hold copies as well, which is why the clan does not immediately force-buy Fang Yuan’s alone.",
        "chapters": [
          106
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "ownership-on-qing-mao-mountain",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "fac_gu_yue_clan"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "During the wolf tide, the medicine hall posts an order for Gu Masters who hold Nine Leaf Vitality Grass to hand copies over for unified production. Fang Yuan is named on the list, and he reads the move as Gu Yue Yao Ji pressuring him while Chi and Mo faction holders already mark “handed over.”",
        "chapters": [
          148
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "ownership-on-qing-mao-mountain",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_gu_yue_yao_ji",
          "fac_mo_family"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Its own direct healing is weak for a rank two Gu. Fang Yuan later treats the continuous sale of vitality leaves as its main advantage, not the grass’s personal heal strength. He also judges the rank two advancement option unsatisfactory, without naming that recipe.",
        "chapters": [
          157
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "trading-away-the-grass",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "After he reaches rank three, Gu Yue Chi Zhong, acting medicine hall elder, offers a Prize Token for the Nine Leaf Vitality Grass. Fang Yuan accepts and transfers the Gu himself so Chi Zhong can refine it quickly.",
        "chapters": [
          157
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "trading-away-the-grass",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_gu_yue_chi_zhong"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "By then Fang Yuan already plans to leave the village, where selling vitality leaves would matter less, and he wants access to the clan’s underground Gu cave through the token.",
        "chapters": [
          157
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "trading-away-the-grass",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "After he trades the grass away, he still lacks a healing Gu he trusts. He names Endless Vitality Gu, Undying Grass, and Self-reliance Gu as rank three healing options he wants, and he notes that the rank two Nine Leaf Vitality Grass healing was not satisfactory even while he held it.",
        "chapters": [
          161
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "trading-away-the-grass",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "sys_healing_gu",
          "gu_vitality_gu",
          "gu_self_reliance_gu"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
